# The librarian (the talk and quests spec, section 6; docs/systems/dialogue.md):
# he stands at his high desk inside his shop off the candle lane, in his ward.
# He keeps the book the curandera wants. The truth, his price or a special way
# gets it; a lie dims him and he refuses, opens on it the next time, and lets
# the stranger make amends (and remembers it after). A bookseller by trade
# (types/bookseller.dialogue): he can be asked for a title and sells books.
# "Librarian" before a line's colon is the name shown in the box, a working
# name: change it here and in name: together.
# Every text is the user's to write; each beat's intent: says what it must do.

== character librarian
name: Librarian
type: bookseller
body: arms_master
colour: #e63833
voice: male_b
intent: the rare-book librarian of the candle lane: exact, courteous, hard to fool; he knows the curandera and what she wants

== beat open_first
when: not(met), not(said(curandera.asked_book))
intent: a stranger in his shop with no errand he knows of: he greets a customer and measures him
Librarian: <<He greets a customer and measures him.>>
> <<Leave.>> -> end

== beat open_after_lie
when: said(lied)
intent: the stranger who lied to him comes back: cold, dim, he says so; the door to amends is open, barely
Librarian [dim]: <<He remembers the lie, and says so.>>
> <<Make amends.>> -> amends
> <<Leave.>> -> end

== beat open_sent
when: said(curandera.asked_book), not(gave(curandera.the_book)), not(has(the_book))
intent: he knows of her: he knows the curandera sent this stranger for the book before he says it
Librarian: <<He knows the curandera sent you, and for what.>>
> <<Tell him the truth: she sent you for the book.>> -> truth
> [if purse>=5] <<Offer to pay him for the book.>> -> pay
> [if said(curandera.asked_book)] ! <<Something only a man of the obsidian could say to him.>> -> special
> <<Lie about why you want the book.>> -> lie
> <<Leave.>> -> end

== beat open
intent: a revisit with no errand left: he is civil; if he forgave a lie, he has not forgotten it
Librarian: <<He nods to a customer he knows.>>
Sense obsidian [if said(forgiven)]: <<He has not forgotten the lie, forgiven or not.>>
> <<Leave.>> -> end

== beat truth
do: give(the_book), mood(+1)
intent: the truth is enough for him: he gives the book freely and says one thing about her, or about it
Librarian [nod]: <<The truth is enough: he gives the book and says one thing about her.>>
-> end

== beat pay
do: charge(5), give(the_book)
intent: he takes the coin (5) and hands over the book, a sale, nothing more
Librarian: <<He takes the coin and hands over the book: a sale, nothing more.>>
-> end

== beat special
do: give(the_book)
intent: the special option struck home: he flares, startled, and gives the book at once
Librarian [flare]: <<Startled, he gives the book at once.>>
-> end

== beat lie
do: set(lied), mood(-1), shade(dim)
intent: he sees through the lie: his light dims, and he refuses the book
Librarian [dim]: <<He sees through the lie, and refuses.>>
-> end

== beat amends
do: clear(lied), set(forgiven), shade(calm)
intent: the stranger makes amends: he accepts it, coolly, and his light steadies; the truth may be told now
Librarian [calm]: <<He accepts the amends, coolly.>>
> [if said(curandera.asked_book), not(gave(curandera.the_book)), not(has(the_book))] <<Tell him the truth now.>> -> truth
> <<Leave.>> -> end

== item the_book
name: <<the curandera's book>>
look: book
intent: the book the curandera wants back from the librarian: what it is, and what it looks like
